WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:06.020
Laying out a laser-optics bench by hand takes weeks. Beamline does it in minutes.

2
00:00:06.770 --> 00:00:11.580
Search arXiv for optical tweezers, pick a real setup figure, and press build.

3
00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:19.700
Three Gemini vision agents read the figure in parallel, while synthesizer, verifier and repair agents stream their reasoning live.

4
00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:26.990
Every design is checked with real physics: Gaussian beams, polarization, and stray-beam laser safety.

5
00:00:27.670 --> 00:00:32.370
Then the parts fly off the drawing onto the bench, and the lasers switch on.

6
00:00:33.330 --> 00:00:38.630
The bench starts misaligned, and the tuner walks each mirror until the power meter climbs back.

7
00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:44.860
You get a cover render and a build document, with a bill of materials and a printable, keyed baseplate.

8
00:00:45.890 --> 00:00:51.950
And it scales: a trapped-ion apparatus with a hundred twenty-one optics, traced in milliseconds.

9
00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:57.050
Beamline. From paper to buildable bench in under three minutes.
